sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design, container runtime (ADR 0250 step 3, docs/reference/task-containers.md): `orbit proof COMMAND --group GROUP` on a group that runs in a task container. The flow and step names are those of docs/cli/proof/proof.mmd. Two things differ: the inner pool is a directory pool, so a restore copies the changed files, and `base` is taken with the nested containers stopped.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: proof
  %% kind: proof.verify
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane TC icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as Author<br/>orbit proof
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve · Swamp Node
  participant TC as Task container<br/>with its fleet
  CLI->>GW: Prove the command<br/>proof COMMAND
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit proof COMMAND`
  %%> - syntax: `orbit proof <command> [--group=<group>]`
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - as for a task VM: the group has its workspace and no other operation running
  opt --group
    Note over GW: Take the named group<br/>caller with Gateway access
    %%> Why:
    %%> - a task container holds no Gateway access, as a task VM holds none, so a Node with Gateway access names the group
  end
  Note over GW: Admit the proof<br/>container · group · inputs
  %%> What it records:
  %%> - the pinned SSH target of the container, the cases file, and the flags `restore_first` and `final_restore`
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>operation ID
  GW->>SW: Start the run<br/>proof-fleet-verify
  SW->>TC: Select the cases<br/>runner plan --lines
  SW->>TC: Restore the base snapshot<br/>restore_first · directory pool
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - `incus snapshot restore` of each nested container inside the task container, then a start, the readiness check and the apply step, as on a VM
  %%> - on a directory pool a restore copies back the files that changed since `base`; the 45 s limit stays, and the build PR measures it
  opt the tokens in base are older than 20 days
    SW->>TC: Re-mint the Swamp tokens<br/>then take base again
    %%> What it does, for a container:
    %%> - the step "Take base again" stops the nested containers, snapshots them and starts them, then the readiness check runs; a snapshot of a running container on a directory pool is not consistent
  end
  loop each batch, in the order of swamp/proof/batches.yaml
    SW->>TC: Run the batch<br/>restore · setup · cases
  end
  SW->>TC: Restore base<br/>final_restore · clean fleet
  Note over SW: Join the verdicts<br/>report step
  alt every case passes and the last restore succeeded
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>verdict per case
    GW-->>CLI: PASS per case<br/>timings
  else a case failed or did not run, or the last restore failed
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>verdict per case
    GW--xCLI: Failed check per case<br/>exit nonzero
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the same codes as on a VM: `proof.cases_failed`, `proof.run_failed`, `proof.restore_failed`
  end
